The debugging exercise is the open-text item whose answers we code for
variation-thinking (\cref{prior-knowledge,mq:agreement}); since every
student describes their steps on the same small program, the answers
are directly comparable, and the analysis program extracts them into a
coding sheet.
The program and its behaviour are shown verbatim in the item body; the
bug is that [[input]] returns a string, so [[price * 3]] repeats the
string instead of multiplying.

